message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Donghyunten (동현텐): a number-pair laboratory in which equal digits or digits summing to ten are cleared, with the Add and Hint allowances set through the esoteric language Donghyun-lang"
type: software
version: "0.1"
date-released: "2026-10-30"
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Dong Hyun
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9883-0229"
    affiliation: "Inha University College of Medicine"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Raspberry-Kim/donghyun-lab6"
url: "https://raspberry-kim.github.io/donghyun-lab6/"
abstract: >-
  Donghyunten is a browser-based, noncommercial number-pair puzzle in the
  tradition of the pen-and-paper game known as Take Ten, Numberama or Seeds.
  Two digits are cleared when they are equal or sum to ten and are joined
  horizontally, vertically or diagonally with only cleared cells between them;
  rows also continue from the end of one line to the start of the next. Add
  rewrites the remaining digits at the end of the board, and Hint shows one
  clearable pair. The only settings, the number of Adds and Hints (0-9 each;
  default 7 and 3), are chosen through a program written in the esoteric
  programming language Donghyun-lang. Scores, emptied rows and cleared boards
  follow a common scheme, and best scores are kept only in the browser. The
  MIT license applies to the Donghyunten code and documentation; the page
  fonts are under the SIL Open Font License. See LICENSE and CREDITS.md.
keywords:
  - number puzzle
  - Take Ten
  - Numberama
  - esoteric programming language
  - JavaScript
